  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Most areas remain dry today...Few showers/storms\ntoday mainly south of the VA/NC border.\n\nAmple sinking/subsidence kicking in behind the upper trough \ntoday as noted by the large dry area above 700mb on the 12z \nRAOB this morning. Better support for storms shifting further \nsouth into the Carolinas/Georgia along a stationary boundary. \nCannot rule out some differential heating low level convergence\nshowers/storms today mainly across our NC counties, but trends \nfavor most of the area staying dry. Not anticipating any severe \nor flooding concerns.\n\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2: Heat returns this coming week.\n\nAbove normal temperatures will be likely this coming week as a\nbroad 5H ridge intensifies over the region. Hot temperatures\narrive by Monday with much of the Piedmont reaching into the mid\n90s, and peaking by Wednesday with highs in the upper 90s in the\neast and upper 80s and low 90s in the mountains. As expected\nwith ridging overhead, limited rain chances expected through\nmuch of the week.",
